  "interpretation_scope": "Spatial correspondence at two near-common-time snapshots only; no causal or convergence claim. The 8.617 microsecond physical-time offset is retained.",
  "spatial_assessment": {
    "summary": "Both global low-pressure cells are nearly pure water and lie about 3.3-3.4 mm downstream of the lamella STL streamwise start, close to the wall and divider-edge geometry. Their nearest transitional-alpha cell centers are 30-39 mm away. The minima at x\u22484.220 m are well downstream of the documented valve-source band x=1.95-2.25 m and valve seat x=2.25 m. Cell widths in min-centered bins are about 12-13.5 mm. In the positive-y sampled band, the median equivalent width changes from 16.9 mm over x=4.16-4.20 m to 13.2 mm over x=4.20-4.22 m, near the divider entrance. The low-pressure cells sit beside the divider edge in liquid, but the interface and a nearby refinement transition cannot be separated as causes by these two snapshots.",
    "divider_reference": "lamella mid-surface STL x-minimum; not a measured plate edge",
    "mesh_width_metric": "cube root of native OpenFOAM cell volume; equivalent width, not an edge length",
    "limitations": [
      "Only two snapshots, offset by 8.616665e-6 s, are compared.",
      "The outer16 global p-min lies at y=-0.3808 m; positive-y thin-band bins characterize a nearby section, not that exact lateral location.",
      "Spatial association does not establish why pressure is low or whether the transient is physical.",
      "Valve source band and seat locations are read from the recorded apparatus inputs; this inspection does not revisit their construction."
    ]
